2026-02-11 01:00:57,947 - _client - INFO: HTTP Request: POST https://dashscope.aliyuncs.com/compatible-mode/v1/chat/completions "HTTP/1.1 200 OK"
2026-02-11 01:00:57,950 - DocumentGraderNode - INFO: Retrieved document What Does a High Equity Risk Premium Mean?

The higher the equity risk premium, the more you will earn from investing in stocks than you would by investing in risk-free assets. This makes investing in stocks more enticing; however, since the equity risk premium is based on historical data, the returns are not guaranteed. is relevant
2026-02-11 01:00:58,575 - _client - INFO: HTTP Request: POST https://dashscope.aliyuncs.com/compatible-mode/v1/chat/completions "HTTP/1.1 200 OK"
2026-02-11 01:00:58,578 - DocumentGraderNode - INFO: Retrieved document Similarly, the equity risk premium refers to the excess return that investing in the stock market provides over a risk-free rate. This excess return compensates investors for taking on the relatively higher risk of equity investing. The size of the premium varies and depends on the level of risk in a particular portfolio. It also changes over time as market risk fluctuates. is relevant
2026-02-11 01:00:59,253 - _client - INFO: HTTP Request: POST https://dashscope.aliyuncs.com/compatible-mode/v1/chat/completions "HTTP/1.1 200 OK"
2026-02-11 01:00:59,256 - DocumentGraderNode - INFO: Retrieved document Key Takeaways

- The equity risk premium is the excess return investors earn over a risk-free rate by investing in the stock market.
- This premium compensates investors for taking on the additional risk associated with stock investments.
- Calculating the equity risk premium often involves historical data and models like the capital asset pricing model.
- The equity risk premium can vary significantly based on market conditions and investor expectations.
- Economists recognize that while the equity risk premium is a valid concept, it is not a guaranteed predictor of future returns. is relevant
